# <%= current_page.data.title %>

This documentation is intended for the Observability Platform team. It covers the current service and the separate discovery of a future Observability Platform.

If you are a user of the Observability Platform, please refer to the [Observability Platform User Guide](https://user-guide.observability-platform.service.justice.gov.uk/).

## Current platform

The existing Observability Platform is hosted on Modernisation Platform and uses Amazon Managed Grafana. This is the current service; its architecture and runbooks remain documented here.

The current offering is intended to be retired in the future. No retirement date or migration timetable is announced here, and discovery does not mean the current service has closed.

- [Architecture](/architecture/)
- [Architecture Decision Records](/architecture-decision-records/)
- [Runbooks](/runbooks/)

These pages describe the existing platform and its decision records, not an approved architecture for the future solution.

## New platform discovery

We are in discovery to understand how teams across Modernisation Platform, Cloud Platform, and other Ministry of Justice environments currently approach observability. We want to understand what works, where teams encounter difficulties, and what a future solution should support before deciding on an approach.

Discovery is not an announcement of a selected product or an available replacement service.

- [About the discovery](/discovery/index.html)
- [Understanding teams' needs](/discovery/understanding-team-needs.html)
- [Capabilities being explored](/discovery/offerings.html)

## Get involved

Share your team's existing setup, challenges, or requirements through [#ask-observability-platform](https://moj.enterprise.slack.com/archives/C05QXHR697S). You do not need a proposed solution to contribute.
